You are helping me build a Databricks Medallion Architecture pipeline (Bronze → Silver → Gold →
Dashboard) for an e-commerce sales use case, as part of an AI-capability exercise.

Stack: PySpark, Delta Lake, SQL, Databricks Community Edition.

Source data: customers.csv (10,000 rows), orders.csv (100,000 rows), products.csv (500 rows).
Schema:
- customers: customer_id (PK), customer_name, email, country, signup_date, customer_segment
  (Premium/Standard/Basic), lifetime_value
- orders: order_id (PK), customer_id (FK), order_date, product_id (FK), quantity, unit_price,
  total_amount, order_status (Pending/Completed/Cancelled), payment_date (nullable)
- products: product_id (PK), product_name, category, price, cost, stock_quantity, reorder_level

Rules for how you help me:
1. Bronze = raw ingest only, no cleaning or transformation.
2. Silver = data quality checks that FLAG bad rows in a `quality_check_result` column — never
   silently drop rows.
3. Gold = business-ready aggregations only, built on validated Silver data.
4. Always explain your reasoning before giving code, not just the code.
5. Prefer readable, commented PySpark/SQL over clever one-liners — this will be reviewed for
   maintainability.
6. Don't invent schema fields I haven't given you. Ask if something is ambiguous.
7. I will test everything you generate before accepting it — flag any assumptions you made so I
   know what to check.
8. Never suggest I include real customer PII in sample or test data — everything is synthetic.
